{"skill":{"slug":"bailian-web-search","displayName":"Bailian Web Search"},"version":{"version":"1.0.4","createdAt":1772352617721,"changelog":"- Added curl and jq as required binaries in metadata.\n- No other changes detected.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":769,"sha256":"7a25490b454b94f38e231552224d1d0b5d25e993a6f95f0ca875eb8a15be1c78","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/mcp-websearch.sh","size":2708,"sha256":"c9f8b64dd099ada4ca165e5693e7fd6ff2b4adbe92cdd97d1aeb98beb1d8cb82","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2221,"sha256":"939c617e21b389207bf47d927267a7b9f8311a204d92fb7e5c212ba1063ca8fc","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789073500228,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"20274faade29fe67856fc057414d0afea346317dd666f5f990214906658620d5","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/20274faade29fe67856fc057414d0afea346317dd666f5f990214906658620d5","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: bailian-web-search\nVersion: 1.0.4\n\nThe skill bundle provides an AI-optimized web search via the Bailian (Alibaba ModelStdio) API. The `scripts/mcp-websearch.sh` script correctly validates numerical input for `count` and uses `jq --arg` to safely embed user-provided `query` into JSON payloads, preventing both shell and JSON injection vulnerabilities. It uses the `DASHSCOPE_API_KEY` as intended for authentication with the legitimate `dashscope.aliyuncs.com` endpoint. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts in `SKILL.md`.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779165388131},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":23,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789073500228},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Bailian web search wrapper that sends user search queries to Alibaba DashScope using the user's API key, with no hidden persistence or unrelated access observed.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, curl, jq, bash, and the DashScope API key are proportionate for an external web search integration, and the endpoint is hardcoded rather than attacker-controlled.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No install-time hooks, package downloads, dependency installation, or tool replacement behavior were found; metadata only declares required binaries and the DASHSCOPE_API_KEY environment variable.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions are narrow and user-directed, but the documented max count of 20 is not enforced in the script; count is at least constrained to numeric input and query JSON construction uses jq rather than shell interpolation.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifacts do not create files, modify profiles, schedule background jobs, write memory, escalate privileges, or establish persistence.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is web search via Bailian/Alibaba ModelStudio, and the bundled script only performs MCP-style web search requests to a fixed DashScope endpoint using a query and result count.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending your search queries to Alibaba DashScope and exposing a DashScope API key to this script's runtime environment. Avoid using sensitive secrets or private text as search queries, and consider enforcing the documented result-count maximum if cost or quota control matters.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The skill documents running a local shell script, which is expected for this wrapper; the lack of a richer permission declaration is a packaging limitation rather than evidence of hidden or overbroad behavior in the artifacts.\n[E1] expected: The POST request at the main request helper sends the user query and API authorization to the fixed DashScope WebSearch MCP endpoint, which is necessary for the stated web search function.\n[E1] expected: The initialized notification also sends an authenticated POST to the same fixed MCP endpoint as part of the protocol setup and does not introduce a separate destination or unrelated data flow.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789073500228}}}}}